Sval: macOS windows can be ordered behind another app's

A link from another app opens over that app, but
LaunchServices activates Sval before delivering the link, and AppKit queues
Sval's key and main windows in front of every other app's as it handles the
activation. SvalMacWindowOrder reads the activation as nsAppShell's
applicationDidBecomeActive: runs, before AppKit commits the window
transaction, and orders those windows behind the app the user was in. It
also gives the chrome nsISvalMacWindowOrder, to bring a window kept behind
forward and to hand activation to the app behind a closing window. Gecko's
widgets only ever order a window in front (nsCocoaWindow::Show, SetFocus),
so no chrome API does this.

